<div role="main" class="pg" id="p-about" style="display: none;"><div class="sec" style="border:0;padding-bottom:0"><h2>About Qivbuild</h2><p>Building consultant and contractor in DHA Phase 8 Lahore 54000 Pakistan Drawing Plan Gray Structure Interior &amp; Renovation</p></div><div class="abw"><div class="abs" id="ab-0"><div class="pic" data-about-img="0" style="background-image:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541888946425-d81bb19240f5?w=800&amp;q=70&amp;fm=webp&amp;auto=format')"></div><div class="abt"><div style="color:var(--bl);font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500">STEP 1</div><h2>Technical Experience <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem"> Experience</span></h2><p>Our work is based on hands-on experience in both building design and site construction We prepare the drawings and then build from them so we know how each detail performs on site: reinforcement placement concrete cover level control and service routing This lets us make accurate design decisions and avoid changes during construction</p><div class="row"><a class="pill f" data-s="ab-1" href="https://qivbuild.site/">Find out more</a><button class="pill" data-m="1">Learn more</button></div></div></div><div class="abs" id="ab-1"><div class="pic" data-about-img="1" style="background-image:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1503387762-592deb58ef4e?w=800&amp;q=70&amp;fm=webp&amp;auto=format')"></div><div class="abt"><div style="color:var(--bl);font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500">STEP 2</div><h2>Project Management <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem"> Project Management</span></h2><p>Project management covers scope drawings material approvals procurement inspections and payments We prepare a construction schedule from the approved drawings and assign a supervisor to each stage Before every concrete pour reinforcement and formwork are checked against the drawings Progress and variations are reported to the owner in writing</p><div class="row"><a class="pill f" data-s="ab-2" href="https://qivbuild.site/">Find out more</a><button class="pill" data-m="1">Learn more</button></div></div></div><div class="abs" id="ab-2"><div class="pic" data-about-img="2" style="background-image:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504307651254-35680f356dfd?w=800&amp;q=70&amp;fm=webp&amp;auto=format')"></div><div class="abt"><div style="color:var(--bl);font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500">STEP 3</div><h2>Team Management <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem"> Team Management</span></h2><p>Our architects structural engineers site engineers supervisors and trade crews work from the same approved drawing set Each role has a defined scope: the architect controls the plan the structural engineer controls member sizes and reinforcement and the site engineer controls execution Instructions are always given from the latest drawing revision which prevents errors caused by outdated drawings</p><div class="row"><a class="pill f" data-s="ab-3" href="https://qivbuild.site/">Find out more</a><button class="pill" data-m="1">Learn more</button></div></div></div><div class="abs" id="ab-3"><div class="pic" data-about-img="3" style="background-image:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?w=800&amp;q=70&amp;fm=webp&amp;auto=format')"></div><div class="abt"><div style="color:var(--bl);font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500">STEP 4</div><h2>Time Management <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem"> Time Management</span></h2><p>Time is planned from the day the drawings are approved Work is sequenced as excavation foundation columns slabs masonry services plaster and finishes with curing and drying time allowed between stages Materials are ordered ahead of each stage so that work is not delayed and the schedule is reviewed weekly against site progress</p><div class="row"><a class="pill f" href="https://qivbuild.site/contact">Find out more</a><button class="pill" data-m="1">Learn more</button></div></div></div></div></div><div role="main" class="pg" id="p-services" style="display: none;"><div id="svc"><div class="rw" id="drawingToggle" style="border:0"><span class="ic"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-job"></use></svg></span><span class="t">Drawing Plan <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem">â€” Building Planning</span></span><span id="drawingArrow"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-ex"></use></svg></span></div><div id="drawingPanel"><div class="ph" id="drawingSlider"><div class="sd" style="background-image:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a73e8,#fbbc04)"><b>Drawing Plan</b><small>Complete drawing set to plot size and local bylaws</small><button class="pill f" data-id="d0">Get in touch</button></div></div><div class="drawing-body"><h2>Drawing Plan â€” Building Planning</h2><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Qivbuild â€” Building Plan Design to Construction</p><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Planning structural design and approval drawings by one team</p><p>A building plan is the technical basis of the whole project It fixes the room layout structural system services routes quantities and approval documents before construction starts At <b>Qivbuild</b> the drawings are prepared by the same team that builds so every dimension is checked for constructability and cost</p><p>Planning starts with the plot: size shape orientation road width soil condition and the applicable bylaws such as plot coverage setbacks maximum height and parking We work within these limits to give you the best usable area natural light and ventilation for your budget</p><h2>What the Drawing Set Includes</h2><ul><li><b>Architectural plans</b> â€” Floor plans elevations sections and room schedules with dimensions door and window sizes and finish levels</li><li><b>Structural drawings</b> â€” Foundation layout column schedule beam and slab reinforcement details and staircase and tank details designed according to the Building Code of Pakistan and recognized structural codes</li><li><b>Electrical plan</b> â€” Load schedule distribution board location circuits switch socket light fan and AC points and earthing</li><li><b>Plumbing plan</b> â€” Water supply lines drainage sewer connection manhole and septic tank locations water tank and pump positions and gas line routing</li><li><b>Approval drawings</b> â€” Submission drawings in the format required by DHA LDA or TMA with the required notes areas and plot details</li><li><b>3D views</b> â€” Exterior and interior views used to confirm design decisions before construction</li></ul><h2>Our Process</h2><p><b>1 Site visit and survey</b> â€” We measure the plot check levels orientation and access and review soil information Your requirements and budget are recorded</p><p><b>2 Concept design</b> â€” Two or three layout options are prepared with areas and circulation so you can select one</p><p><b>3 Detailed drawings</b> â€” After the concept is approved we prepare the architectural structural electrical and plumbing drawings and a bill of quantities</p><p><b>4 Approval and construction</b> â€” Drawings are submitted to the authority After approval the same team builds exactly to the approved drawings</p><h2>Why Qivbuild for Planning</h2><p>Our drawings are prepared with site experience so they work in practice: practical column positions correct stair and room dimensions workable service routes and accurate quantities This reduces changes material waste and cost overruns during construction</p><p>We plan 5 Marla 10 Marla 1 Kanal and commercial plots in DHA Phase 8 and across Lahore One team handles design and construction so there is no gap between the drawing and the work on site</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="pill f" href="https://qivbuild.site/contact">Get in touch</a><a class="pill" href="https://qivbuild.site/gallery?cat=plan">See Photos</a><a class="pill" href="tel:+923430107773">Call Now</a><a class="pill" href="https://wa.me/923430107773">WhatsApp</a></div></div></div><div class="rw" id="grayToggle" style="border:0"><span class="ic"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-job"></use></svg></span><span class="t">Gray Structure <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem">â€” Structural Construction</span></span><span id="grayArrow"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-ex"></use></svg></span></div><div id="grayPanel"><div class="ph" id="graySlider"><div class="sd" style="background-image:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a73e8,#fbbc04)"><b>Gray Structure</b><small>Foundation to slab built to structural drawings</small><button class="pill f" data-id="d1">Get in touch</button></div></div><div class="drawing-body"><h2>Gray Structure â€” Structural Construction</h2><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Qivbuild â€” Structural Construction to Drawings</p><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Gray structure = foundation frame slabs and masonry before finishing</p><p>Gray structure is the complete structural work of the building up to the finishing stage: excavation foundation columns beams slabs staircases and brick masonry with plaster and services rough-in Its quality decides the safety and service life of the building so it is built strictly to the structural drawings</p><p>Errors at this stage are costly to correct later We therefore check reinforcement formwork levels and alignment before every concrete pour and record the checks</p><h2>Scope of Gray Structure</h2><ul><li><b>Excavation and foundation</b> â€” Excavation to the designed depth compaction plain concrete (PCC) and reinforced footings or raft as per the foundation design</li><li><b>Columns</b> â€” Reinforcement as per the column schedule correct lap lengths and stirrup spacing with plumb checked before pouring</li><li><b>Beams and slabs</b> â€” Formwork bar bending to the drawings concrete cover and placement of electrical conduits and plumbing sleeves before casting</li><li><b>Brick masonry</b> â€” Wall thickness and bonding as per drawings vertical alignment and openings at the designed sizes and levels</li><li><b>Staircase and water tanks</b> â€” Reinforced concrete staircases and underground and overhead tanks with waterproofing</li><li><b>Damp-proofing and waterproofing</b> â€” Damp-proof course at plinth level and waterproofing of roof bathrooms and tanks</li></ul><h2>Gray Structure Process</h2><p><b>1 Excavation and foundation</b> â€” Setting out from the drawings excavation to the designed depth soil check PCC and foundation concrete</p><p><b>2 Columns and beams</b> â€” Reinforcement fixing shuttering and concrete with level and plumb checks at each stage</p><p><b>3 Slab and masonry</b> â€” Slab casting with proper compaction and brickwork under daily supervision</p><p><b>4 Quality control</b> â€” Concrete cube tests slump tests reinforcement checks and a minimum of 7 days of curing</p><h2>Why Qivbuild for Gray Structure</h2><p>We use cement and steel from approved manufacturers follow the specified mix and reinforcement quantities and do not substitute materials without the engineer approval Material receipts and test results are available to the owner</p><p>Because the same team prepared the drawings questions on site are resolved quickly and correctly and the building is constructed exactly as designed</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="pill f" href="https://qivbuild.site/contact">Get in touch</a><a class="pill" href="https://qivbuild.site/gallery?cat=gray">See Photos</a><a class="pill" href="tel:+923430107773">Call Now</a><a class="pill" href="https://wa.me/923430107773">WhatsApp</a></div></div></div><div class="rw" id="interiorToggle" style="border:0"><span class="ic"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-job"></use></svg></span><span class="t">Interior Design <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem">â€” Finishing and Fit-out</span></span><span id="interiorArrow"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-ex"></use></svg></span></div><div id="interiorPanel"><div class="ph" id="interiorSlider"><div class="sd" style="background-image:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a73e8,#fbbc04)"><b>Interior Design</b><small>Space planning kitchens bathrooms joinery and lighting</small><button class="pill f" data-id="d2">Get in touch</button></div></div><div class="drawing-body"><h2>Interior Design â€” Finishing and Fit-out</h2><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Qivbuild â€” Functional Interior Planning and Finishing</p><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Interior design coordinated with the building services</p><p>Interior design covers the planning and finishing of all internal spaces: room layouts furniture positions kitchen and bathroom design joinery ceilings flooring lighting and colours We design the interior together with the building services so that electrical points plumbing and AC are placed correctly before walls are finished</p><p>Interior work is planned from measured dimensions so cabinets doors and fixtures fit without adjustment on site</p><h2>Scope of Interior Work</h2><ul><li><b>Living and lounge areas</b> â€” Furniture layout based on room dimensions and circulation with sockets lighting TV and AC points placed accordingly</li><li><b>Kitchen</b> â€” Work-triangle layout counter heights storage exhaust and electrical and plumbing points for appliances</li><li><b>Bedrooms</b> â€” Wardrobe and bed layout ceiling and lighting design and window placement for natural light and privacy</li><li><b>Bathrooms</b> â€” Tile layout waterproofing slope to drains sanitary fixture positions and ventilation</li><li><b>Lighting</b> â€” General task and accent lighting plans with switching layout and load calculation</li><li><b>Finishes</b> â€” Flooring wall finishes false ceilings paint doors and joinery with material specifications</li></ul><h2>Interior Design Process</h2><p><b>1 Requirement brief</b> â€” Family size usage and budget are recorded and rooms are measured on site</p><p><b>2 3D layout</b> â€” Layouts and 3D views are prepared and revised before work begins</p><p><b>3 Materials and execution</b> â€” Tiles marble wood and paint are specified with quantities and work proceeds room by room under supervision</p><h2>Why Qivbuild for Interior Design</h2><p>Interior work is carried out by the same team that built the structure so concealed pipes conduits and structural elements are known and accounted for in the design Finishes are chosen to match your budget and the way each room will be used</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="pill f" href="https://qivbuild.site/contact">Get in touch</a><a class="pill" href="https://qivbuild.site/gallery?cat=interior">See Photos</a><a class="pill" href="tel:+923430107773">Call Now</a><a class="pill" href="https://wa.me/923430107773">WhatsApp</a></div></div></div><div class="rw" id="exteriorToggle" style="border:0"><span class="ic"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-job"></use></svg></span><span class="t">Exterior Design <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem">â€” Elevation and Facade</span></span><span id="exteriorArrow"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-ex"></use></svg></span></div><div id="exteriorPanel"><div class="ph" id="exteriorSlider"><div class="sd" style="background-image:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a73e8,#fbbc04)"><b>Exterior Design</b><small>Elevation facade boundary wall gate and weatherproofing</small><button class="pill f" data-id="d3">Get in touch</button></div></div><div class="drawing-body"><h2>Exterior Design â€” Elevation and Facade</h2><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Qivbuild â€” Elevation Design and Weather Protection</p><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Elevation facade boundary and drainage detailed with the structure</p><p>Exterior design covers the elevation facade materials boundary wall gate landscaping and outdoor lighting The elevation is designed together with the floor plans so that window sizes floor heights and structural members match the front design</p><p>The exterior is also the weather protection of the building Facade finishes roof drainage and waterproofing are detailed to protect the structure from rain sun and moisture</p><h2>Scope of Exterior Work</h2><ul><li><b>Front elevation</b> â€” Elevation drawings and 3D views in modern classical or other styles chosen by the owner with dimensions and material notes</li><li><b>Paint and texture</b> â€” Weather-resistant exterior paint and texture finishes with surface preparation specified</li><li><b>Main gate and boundary wall</b> â€” Gate pillar and wall design with foundation and structural details</li><li><b>Lawn and landscaping</b> â€” Lawn paving driveway and drainage layout</li><li><b>Outdoor lighting</b> â€” Facade gate and boundary lighting plan with fixtures and circuits</li><li><b>Waterproofing and drainage</b> â€” Roof slope rainwater pipes damp-proof courses and sealing of joints</li></ul><h2>Exterior Design Process</h2><p><b>1 Site and context study</b> â€” Plot street orientation and neighbouring buildings are reviewed to select the elevation style</p><p><b>2 3D elevation</b> â€” Elevation views are prepared showing colours stone and lighting before construction</p><p><b>3 Execution</b> â€” Materials are specified to quality standards and installed under supervision</p><h2>Why Qivbuild for Exterior Design</h2><p>The exterior and interior are designed together with the structure so the facade is built into the structural and service plan instead of added afterwards One team handles the work from design to construction</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="pill f" href="https://qivbuild.site/contact">Get in touch</a><a class="pill" href="https://qivbuild.site/gallery?cat=exterior">See Photos</a><a class="pill" href="tel:+923430107773">Call Now</a><a class="pill" href="https://wa.me/923430107773">WhatsApp</a></div></div></div><div class="rw" id="renovationToggle" style="border:0"><span class="ic"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-job"></use></svg></span><span class="t">Renovation <span style="color:var(--mut);font-weight:400;font-size:0.85rem">â€” Repair and Remodelling</span></span><span id="renovationArrow"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-ex"></use></svg></span></div><div id="renovationPanel"><div class="ph" id="renovationSlider"><div class="sd" style="background-image:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a73e8,#fbbc04)"><b>Renovation</b><small>Condition survey repair services upgrade and remodelling</small><button class="pill f" data-id="d4">Get in touch</button></div></div><div class="drawing-body"><h2>Renovation â€” Repair and Remodelling</h2><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Qivbuild â€” Assessment Repair and Remodelling of Existing Buildings</p><p style="color:var(--bl);font-weight:600">Condition survey first then repair upgrade and remodelling</p><p>Renovation improves an existing building by repairing defects upgrading services and changing the layout or finishes We start with a condition survey so the scope and cost are based on what the building actually needs Cracks dampness leakage and outdated wiring and plumbing are identified before any work is priced</p><p>Structural alterations such as removing walls or adding a floor are checked by a structural engineer before work begins so the building remains safe</p><h2>Scope of Renovation</h2><ul><li><b>Condition survey</b> â€” Inspection of structure walls roof plumbing and electrical systems with a written report and photographs</li><li><b>Repair</b> â€” Crack repair damp and seepage treatment roof waterproofing and replacement of damaged wiring and pipes</li><li><b>Remodelling</b> â€” Changing room sizes relocating kitchens and bathrooms and opening or closing walls with structural checks</li><li><b>Finishes upgrade</b> â€” New flooring tiles paint ceilings doors and lighting</li><li><b>Strengthening and additions</b> â€” Column and beam strengthening and new floors or extensions designed and checked against the existing foundation</li><li><b>Full renovation</b> â€” Complete work from structure to finishing when the building needs a comprehensive upgrade</li></ul><h2>Renovation Process</h2><p><b>1 Survey and estimate</b> â€” The building is inspected defects are listed and a cost estimate is given before work begins</p><p><b>2 Renovation plan</b> â€” Drawings show what is removed retained and added with a schedule and sequence of work</p><p><b>3 Execution</b> â€” Work proceeds in sections with dust and debris control and regular progress updates</p><h2>Why Qivbuild for Renovation</h2><p>We carry out both design and construction so the existing structure services and new work are coordinated Scope cost and schedule are agreed in writing before work starts</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="pill f" href="https://qivbuild.site/contact">Get in touch</a><a class="pill" href="https://qivbuild.site/gallery?cat=renovation">See Photos</a><a class="pill" href="tel:+923430107773">Call Now</a><a class="pill" href="https://wa.me/923430107773">WhatsApp</a></div></div></div></div></div>
